# found-footy Caddy fragment (Go rebuild).
#
# ────── STATUS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This file is NOT read by the workspace Caddy yet. The workspace proxy
# currently uses "Option 1" from ~/workspace/proxy/CONVENTIONS.md:
# per-project fragments live centrally at
# ~/workspace/proxy/caddy/caddy.d/<project>.caddy. See
# ~/workspace/vedanta-dhobley/docs/todo.md § "Deferred — migrate per-
# project Caddy config to Option 2" for the eventual migration.
#
# Until that migration lands, this file is documentation of the routing
# the Go rebuild will need. Every block is commented out so it can't
# accidentally take effect if someone runs Option 2 prematurely.
#
# Real prod routing (Python found-footy) lives untouched at
# ~/workspace/proxy/caddy/caddy.d/found-footy.caddy. This file does NOT
# supersede that until cutover; do not copy blocks from here to the
# prod fragment until the corresponding Go service is running.
#
# Uncomment each block during Phase S when its underlying service
# actually exists + is running (§16.5 O phases).

# ────── prod (post-cutover) ───────────────────────────────────────────────

## Go API — typed HTTP read surface + share-id redirect (SSE is
## vedanta-systems'). Port :8081 = Chi read API; :8080 is internal metrics.
## Uncomment in Phase C cutover (§16.10) once verified in prod.
# http://found-footy-prod-api.{$BASE_DOMAIN} {
#     reverse_proxy found-footy-prod-api:8081
# }

## Temporal UI — swaps in for the existing Python-era fragment at
## cutover. The Python fragment is deleted at the same PR.
# http://found-footy-prod-temporal-ui.{$BASE_DOMAIN} {
#     reverse_proxy found-footy-prod-temporal-ui:8080
# }

## Garage admin UI — hostname vs reverse_proxy target must be
## byte-identical per CONVENTIONS. Decision deferred to Phase C per
## §10 (either sub-route on the primary garage hostname, or a dedicated
## garage-web container).
# http://found-footy-prod-garage-web.{$BASE_DOMAIN} {
#     reverse_proxy found-footy-prod-garage-web:3902
# }

## Twitter noVNC — gated behind the `vnc` compose profile in prod
## (manual cookie re-auth). Only reachable when that profile is active.
# http://found-footy-prod-twitter-vnc.{$BASE_DOMAIN} {
#     reverse_proxy found-footy-prod-twitter-vnc:6080
# }

# ────── dev (used during Phase S onward) ──────────────────────────────────

## Go API dev — target for vedanta-systems dev to point at during the
## rebuild. Read API on :8081 (#167 shipped). The ACTIVE dev entry lives in
## the proxy stack's found-footy.caddy; this is the documentation copy.
# http://found-footy-dev-api.{$BASE_DOMAIN} {
#     reverse_proxy found-footy-dev-api:8081
# }

## Temporal UI dev — uncomment as soon as the dev stack goes up
## routinely (early Phase S).
# http://found-footy-dev-temporal-ui.{$BASE_DOMAIN} {
#     reverse_proxy found-footy-dev-temporal-ui:8080
# }

## Garage admin dev.
# http://found-footy-dev-garage-web.{$BASE_DOMAIN} {
#     reverse_proxy found-footy-dev-garage-web:3902
# }

## Twitter noVNC dev — always on (no `vnc` profile in dev per §10);
## uncomment when the twitter binary actually starts a browser.
# http://found-footy-dev-twitter.{$BASE_DOMAIN} {
#     reverse_proxy found-footy-dev-twitter:6080
# }
